Make one, then make this edit there:

    git -C '<tmp>/with space' worktree add '<tmp>/with space-edit-my-file' -b edit-my-file

The file is then '<tmp>/with space-edit-my-file/my file.py'. (If that folder or branch already exists, pick another name.)
Turning the guard off is the person's call (/bendit:adopt --detailed), not yours.

